id: pm-cqddvl
title: pm gc --scope runtime removes derived caches through a redirected runtime directory
description: "Raised by the Codex review of the pm-gh1664 change on 2026-11-20. The runtime gc scope removes registry targets such as runtime/test-runs, runtime/history-drift-cache.json and, since pm-gh1664, runtime/history-stream-summary.json by joining them under the tracker root and removing them. If runtime/ is a symbolic link or Windows junction, the removal follows it and deletes files outside the tracker. The new stream summary's own reads and writes already refuse a redirected runtime directory (lstat must report a real directory), as does the context-usage ledger (src/sdk/context/usage-ledger.ts, docs/BOUNDED_CONTEXT_READS.md), but the gc registry path predates that rule and applies to every runtime target. Duplicate check: searched gc runtime, redirected runtime, symlink, junction and gc follow; no item owns it."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[4]: gc,runtime,safety,symlink
created_at: "2026-11-20T13:55:29.388Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-20T20:54:58.185Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-20T16:12:40.631Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-20T16:12:40.631Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: pm gc refuses to remove any runtime-scope target when runtime/ is not a real directory (lstat) and reports a warning naming the redirected directory; existing removals of real runtime targets are unchanged; a spec covers a symlinked runtime directory
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: low
confidence: medium
severity: low
resolution: "runGc checks once, by lstat, whether runtime/ is a real directory. When it is a symbolic link, junction or file, every runtime-scope target and the workspace snapshot temp sweep are retained, and gc reports redirected_runtime_directory:runtime. A failure to inspect runtime/ other than its absence is rethrown."
expected_result: Garbage collection never deletes outside the tracker
actual_result: "A symlinked runtime directory keeps its link target's test-runs, history-drift-cache.json and history-stream-summary.json, and gc warns; real runtime directories are cleaned as before (gc spec 21/21)"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-gh1664,discovered_from,"2026-11-20T13:55:29.388Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-20T18:22:21.083Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 17 (PR #1761, head e27e5636b): gc checked runtime/ only once, but each target's extension read hook runs before that target is removed, so a hook or a concurrent migration could redirect runtime/ in between. removeCacheFile now re-checks runtime/ after the read hook, immediately before removing each runtime target, and gc checks again before the snapshot temp sweep, since the last target's write hooks run after its own check. Specs redirect runtime/ from the first target's read hook and from the last target's write hook. In both, nothing in the other tracker is removed and gc warns redirected_runtime_directory:runtime."
  "2026-11-20T20:54:58.185Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 23 (PR #1761, head bebbdbe35): gc inspected every cache target with fs.stat, which follows links, so a circular or dangling link at a target path (for example runtime/history-stream-summary.json) made pm gc abort with ELOOP before its later scopes, even in dry-run mode. removeCacheFile now inspects targets with lstat, so a target that is a link is retained with not_a_file or not_a_directory, and the remaining scopes still run. A spec places a circular link at the summary path and runs gc with scope runtime,locks, dry-run and real: the link survives, the warning is reported and the locks summary is present. docs/COMMANDS.md states the no-follow rule for the runtime scope."
